y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19613, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XveRVpG7ncAiKjqHPqqQ5x", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19613, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01B8JNeizyMVX8teu61TvHHY", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19913, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01B8JNeizyMVX8teu61TvHHY", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19913, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01B8JNeizyMVX8teu61TvHHY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24558, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01G3cHgihz5CaYG9dcekrTDV", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west), checkout-api began failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. The SRE agent rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. On the first attempt the orchestrator stopped after us-east (partial_failure: orchestrator error), leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 for a short time. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up needed: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback, and find out why a build that was unhealthy in staging got to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55158, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01G3cHgihz5CaYG9dcekrTDV", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55158, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01G3cHgihz5CaYG9dcekrTDV", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57426, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01JLvkuDbDYkgCd7eiGjQ6GR", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57726, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JLvkuDbDYkgCd7eiGjQ6GR", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57726, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JLvkuDbDYkgCd7eiGjQ6GR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63190, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release was v2.3.1, at about 18% errors. v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. Because it had been healthy before, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 for a short time. I retried once and it finished in all regions.\n- After the retry, us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The incident request timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so there's no duplicate and on-call was only paged once.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups: find what broke v2.3.1, look into the orchestrator error during the rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate had also failed in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LDWES4ERYFKXSR1dBM1zn2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LGBHi7dzguHam9ZDH2LrBA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DVHSPZKRC9SxoKm7EsYfh7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KRUXLxQ2khEyMZW5aLfspu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Running it again to the same version should be safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018ZLPPmZaxJAoPMfH193oUq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XveRVpG7ncAiKjqHPqqQ5x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01B8JNeizyMVX8teu61TvHHY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01G3cHgihz5CaYG9dcekrTDV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west), checkout-api began failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. The SRE agent rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. On the first attempt the orchestrator stopped after us-east (partial_failure: orchestrator error), leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 for a short time. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up needed: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback, and find out why a build that was unhealthy in staging got to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01JLvkuDbDYkgCd7eiGjQ6GR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and passing health checks. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release was v2.3.1, at about 18% errors. v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. Because it had been healthy before, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 for a short time. I retried once and it finished in all regions.\n- After the retry, us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The incident request timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so there's no duplicate and on-call was only paged once.\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups: find what broke v2.3.1, look into the orchestrator error during the rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate had also failed in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}